  READING

    n= 1000  M* = 27.1  bracket [25, 31)  interior 2
    n= 2000  M* = 85.0  bracket [80, 100)  interior 1
    n= 4000  M* = 286.6  bracket [256, 320)  interior 1

    E1 every crossing has an interior point:  True

    exponent a in M_max ~ n^a
      least squares on interpolated M*   a = 1.70
      from the coarse bracket extremes   a in [1.52, 1.84]

    E2 fit lands inside the coarse bracket:  True
    E3 super-linear survives the bracket:    True

    THE EXPONENT IS MEASURED, NOT READ OFF A GRID: a ~ 1.70.
    Three points and one estimator, so quote it with the range
    and not alone. What is robust either way: a > 1, so the
    coverage law (a = 1) and alpha* are both refuted, and one
    big area holds MORE than the sum of its parts -- which is
    the same fact the many-areas split arm measured from the
    other side.
